---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Footprints — Sanmarg : Aparajita" description="Footprints — Aparajita, an initiative by Sanmarg.">
<section>
        <div class="container sec-pad">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-12">
                       <span class="inside-header">
                           <h1>Footprints</h1>
                       </span>
                   </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
<section class="sec-pad grad-bg">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-10 mx-auto">
                    <p class="text-center intro-text mt-3 quote-font">
                        She is making <b>footprints</b> that we believe will brave the test of time. She is steadfast in <b>supporting her tribe</b>. Aparajita is on a mission to bring women of excellence closer to <b>fulfilling their destiny</b>.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sec-pad">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-12">
                    <div class="row d-flex align-items-center">
                        <div class="col-sm-7">
                            <p>Apart from extending financial assistance to women in education for the underprivileged such as Reba Murmu (who runs a school in a Santal village), Aparajita routinely donates school bags, stationery, and winter wear for children. In 2020, during the COVID-19 pandemic, she provided monetary donations to various NGOs to assist them in their relief efforts. In 2023, she donated INR 50,000 per winner per category to causes that her awardees believe in, such as Nishtha, an outstanding women’s NGO.</p>
                            <p>She has collaborated with the women of Humtree, a small-batch, community-made fair trade brand that champions the cause of preserving the Sunderbans. Humtree manufactured sustainable crochet bags which were made available at the Aparajita ceremony to her esteemed guests.</p>
                            <div id="landing">
                                <p>She also extends unconditional media support through Sanmarg for all our nominees and jury members, helping to amplify their stories and achievements. Through initiatives like &#8220;Kadam Haat,&#8221; she offers free columns in Sanmarg to promote and support women artisans, empowering them economically.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-sm-1"></div>
                        <div class="col-sm-4 mob-img">
                            <img src="/images/foot-print-motif.webp" class="img-fluid" alt="Footprint">
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-12 content-gap">
                    <div class="row d-flex align-items-center">
                        <div class="col-sm-7 px-5 odr-mob">
                            <div id="footprintTwoIntro">
                                <div id="landingTitle">
                                    <h2 class="sub-hdr my-3">Sprinter Dadi &#8211; Bhagwani Devi Dagar</h2>
                                </div>
                                <p><span class="fw-bold">“Sports isn’t just about having fun &#8211; it can be about changing lives and making your country proud,”</span> says the nonagenarian athlete and pride of India.</p>
                                <p><button class="theme-btn theme-btn-light" id="footprintTwoReadMoreBtn" onclick="myFunction1()">Read More</button></p>
                            </div>
                            <div id="fullFootprintTwo" style="display:none">
                                <h2 class="sub-hdr my-3">Sprinter Dadi &#8211; Bhagwani Devi Dagar</h2>
                                <p><span class="fw-bold">“Sports isn’t just about having fun &#8211; it can be about changing lives and making your country proud,”</span> says the nonagenarian athlete and pride of India. Aparajita felicitated her with a Jury Award in Sports in 2022. She has since then humbly served as the sole facilitator for Dadi’s journey to Torun, Poland in 2023 for the World Masters Athletics Indoor Championships. Here, she won 3 golds for India. Dadi has also gone on to secure a Guinness World Record, and has garnered international acclaim for herself and the nation. Aparajita is proud to have given wings to her dreams.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
